Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-18 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved) for the model store (LIBRARY.md "The model store") and the 3D
exports (the 3D spec on the site, docs/superpowers/specs/
2026-11-16-3d-exports-design.md, section 8.4). A two layer board, 20 by 15 mm
(an Edge.Cuts rectangle), with two footprints and three model lines:
- R1, Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric, one library model line,
  ${KICAD10_3DMODEL_DIR}/Resistor_SMD.3dshapes/R_0603_1608Metric.step: its
  body is fetched from the model store, never committed here (kicad-packages3D,
  CC BY-SA 4.0 with KiCad's libraries exception);
- U1, a footprint of the board's own (models3d-small:Blocks), two lines:
  ${KIPRJMOD}/cube.step and ${KIPRJMOD}/block.wrl, the second answered by its
  same stem STEP sibling block.step (no block.wrl exists, on purpose).
cube.step (1.6 by 1.6 by 1.6 mm) and block.step (2.4 by 1.2 by 1.6 mm) are
boards alone, written by kicad-cli 10.0.4 in the kicad/kicad:10.0.4 image from
the hand boards in make/ (an Edge.Cuts rectangle each, 1.6 mm thick):
  kicad-cli pcb export step --board-only --force -o cube.step make/cube.kicad_pcb
  kicad-cli pcb export step --board-only --force -o block.step make/block.kicad_pcb
A STEP export of the board with its components holds three bodies beside the
board's. files.json lists what the e2e harness opens. The KiCad files carry
no comment (their formats have none), so this file holds their license.
For tests/e2e/models3d.spec.ts.
